# `SUBJECT-VOCABULARY-SCOPE`/`SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`: `flowchart` declares exactly ONE subject word of
# its own — `external` — and it must still parse. The WITHDRAW half of the
# grid for this genre is 243.
#
# The referent is ISO 5807 §9.4.2 *Terminator*, "the exit to, or entry from,
# the outside world", and this is the divergence the shared text hid: it is
# NOT `block`'s referent, which is a generic out-of-figure endpoint with no
# source standard at all. The spelling is FigDown's, not ISO's, and it stays
# for a reason that only exists inside this genre — the rename ISO points to
# COLLIDES with `terminator`, which is already this genre's live role
# keyword (`FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS`). So ISO has no word left for the never-drawn variant, which
# is stated rather than papered over.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
terminator start "Request received"
process apply "Apply change"
external audit "Audit store"
flowline start -> apply
flowline apply -> audit
